CHEYENNE WYOMING:
Section1.
That various sections of Chapter 5.52, Massage Establishments, of Title
5, Business Licenses and Regulations, of the code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, are
hereby amended as setoutin this ordinance.
5.52.130
Denial, suspension or revocation of license or permit.
A.
Denial.Within ten (10) days of the denial of an application for a massage
business establishment license, or massage therapist permit, the applicant may file with the city
clerk a written request for a hearing before the-governing body in accordance with Chapter
2.92, Administrative Hearing Procedure.At the hearing, to be held at a reasonable time after
receipt of request, evidence will be received for the purpose of determining whether the denial
should be upheld; the notification of and reason for such decisions shall be set forth in writing
andsent-to the-applicant by means of registered or certified mail or hand delivery.Duringthe
hearing all requirements of the Wyoming Administrative Procedure Aet shall be followed.
Suspension or Revocation. Any massage business establishment license, or
provision of this chapter, or for grounds that would warrant the denial of the issuance of such
license or permit in the first instance, orfor the violation of any lawrelating to or regulating
massage business establishments or massage therapists.
Except in cases of emergeney health-and/or safety-reasons, as defined by the
city/county health director, the suspension or revocation of a license or permit will be
accomplished pursuantto a hearing heldbefore-the-governing body at which time evidence
will be received for the purpose of determining whether the license or permit should be
suspended, revoked or retained. Following the hearing; if the-license-or permit is suspended or
